; Sample one pin, one bit per clock, into a 32-bit word.
;
; That is the whole program. Timing EDGES in PIO needs a counting loop whose
; cycle cost has to be right in every branch, and a miscount is a wrong bit rate
; that looks plausible. Sampling has no branches: every bit costs exactly one
; clock, autopush hands off a word every 32, and the run lengths are recovered
; on the CPU where they can be checked.
;
; At 125 MHz that is 8 ns per sample -- 15 samples across the shortest bit a
; CAN FD bus can carry (125 ns at 8 Mbit), and 500 across a 250k bit.
.program cansample
.wrap_target
    in pins, 1
.wrap
